            <ArticleTitle>The Vegetarian Habit in Italy: Prevalence and Characteristics of Consumers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/03670244.2014.1001981</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many individuals around the world follow vegetarian diet. The aim of this study was to examine the variables associated to a vegetarian diet. Data were drawn from the national cross-sectional survey &quot;Health and use of health care in Italy&quot;. Vegetarian habit was prevalent in 0.79% of sample, mainly females. Multivariate model has confirmed the association between vegetarianism and females, age, level of education, marital status separated/divorced/single, diabetes, bad state of perceived health. Little to no research has been conducted in this area until now. As for all types of diet, the vegetarian one should be controlled.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
